# Clean Architecture — Bardak

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Contains | MUST NOT import |
|-------|----------|-----------------|
| `domain/` | Entities, abstract repositories, use cases | Flutter, `dart:ui`, data layer |
| `data/` | Models, data sources (Hive/Firestore/SharedPrefs), repository impls | presentation layer |
| `presentation/` | BLoCs/Cubits, pages, widgets | repositories, data sources directly |

Presentation depends on **UseCases only**. Never inject a repository into a BLoC.

## Feature Folder Structure

Every full-stack feature MUST follow:

```
feature_x/
  domain/
    entities/
    repositories/      # abstract interface class
    usecases/
  data/
    data_sources/
      local/
      remote/
    repositories/      # impl
  presentation/
    bloc/
    pages/
    widgets/
  feature_x_scope.dart # GetIt registration for this feature
```

Presentation-only features (home, splash, rules) may omit domain/data layers.
Game-loop features (game_session, card_round, single_word_round) may use domain entities
directly in BLoCs when there is no persistence layer.

## Canonical Example

```
word_pack/
  domain/repositories/word_packs_repository.dart     # abstract interface class
  domain/usecases/get_word_packs_usecase.dart
  data/data_sources/word_packs_local_data_source.dart
  data/repositories/word_packs_repository_impl.dart
  presentation/bloc/word_packs_bloc.dart
  word_packs_scope.dart
```

## Naming Conventions

- Repository interfaces: `*Repository` (abstract interface class)
- Repository impls: `*RepositoryImpl`
- Data sources: `*LocalDataSource` / `*RemoteDataSource`
- Use cases: `*UseCase` with a `Params` class in the same file
- Entities: `*Entity`
